manual stats entered by the coach, spatial data from the CV service, analysis by Claude.</footer>
</div></body></html>`;

/* ── cache ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
const payload = {
  status: 'done',
  match_id: profile.match_id,
  opponent: profile.opponent,
  date: profile.date,
  degraded: profile.degraded,
  cv_error: profile.cv_error,
  generated_at: new Date().toISOString(),
  team,
  players,
  cv: profile.cv,
};

const store = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');
store.reports = store.reports || {};
store.reports[profile.match_id] = { ...payload, html };

// Bounded, so a day of demo runs cannot grow the stored data without limit.
const keys = Object.keys(store.reports);
if (keys.length > 25) keys.slice(0, keys.length - 25).forEach((k) => delete store.reports[k]);

return [{ json: { ...payload, club_id: profile.club_id, supabase_url: profile.supabase_url, html } }];

/* 12 — Report endpoint: GET /report?match_id=...
 *
 * Served from workflow static data, which node 11 writes at the end of a run.
 * A cache miss falls through to Supabase, so a report survives an n8n restart —
 * but the demo never depends on the database being up.
 */
// Keep in step with SUPABASE_URL in the Normalize node. This branch has its own
// trigger, so it cannot read that node's output.
const SUPABASE_URL = 'https://tifynfruqgkbuiyiljfb.supabase.co';

const q = $input.first().json.query || {};
const matchId = (q.match_id || '').trim();

if (!matchId) {
  return [{ json: { found: true, status: 'error', error: 'match_id query parameter is required' } }];
}

const hit = ($getWorkflowStaticData('global').reports || {})[matchId];
if (hit) {
  const { html, ...report } = hit;   // the HTML is served separately, not inlined here
  return [{ json: { found: true, source: 'n8n', ...report } }];
}

return [{ json: { found: false, match_id: matchId, status: 'processing', stage: 'claude', supabase_url: SUPABASE_URL } }];

/* 12b — cache miss: rebuild the response from Supabase.
 *
 * Reads the v_match_report view (db/schema.sql), which folds team_reports,
 * reports and player_match_stats into one row per match. If the database is not
 * configured or the match is not there yet, answer "processing" — the frontend
 * polls, so an honest not-yet is the right answer, never a fabricated report.
 */
const req = $('12 Lookup report').first().json;
const rows = $input.all().map((i) => i.json).filter((r) => r && r.match_id && r.team);

if (!rows.length) {
  return [{ json: { status: 'processing', stage: 'claude', match_id: req.match_id, source: 'supabase' } }];
}

const row = rows[0];
const cvPlayers = Array.isArray(row.cv_players) ? row.cv_players.filter((p) => p.heatmap_url || p.avg_position) : [];

return [{
  json: {
    status: 'done',
    source: 'supabase',
    match_id: row.match_id,
    degraded: cvPlayers.length === 0,
    team: row.team,
    players: Array.isArray(row.players) ? row.players : [],
    cv: cvPlayers.length ? { players: cvPlayers } : null,
  },
}];

/* 11b — GET /report-html?match_id=...  serves the rendered report as a page.
 *
 * This is the shareable artifact: one link a coach can open on a phone with no
 * frontend, no build step and no network beyond the heatmap images.
 */
const q = $input.first().json.query || {};
const matchId = (q.match_id || '').trim();
const hit = ($getWorkflowStaticData('global').reports || {})[matchId];

if (hit && hit.html) return [{ json: { html: hit.html } }];

const esc = (s) => String(s ?? '').replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]));
return [{
  json: {
    html: `<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Report not ready</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#0b1014;color:#dce7ee;font:15px/1.6 ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;
display:grid;place-items:center;min-height:100vh;text-align:center;padding:24px}
code{background:#16222a;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:5px}</style></head>
<body><div><h1>Not ready</h1>
<p>No report is cached for <code>${esc(matchId || '(no match_id)')}</code>.</p>
<p style="color:#8ba0ae">Either the run has not finished yet, or this n8n instance restarted after it did.
The durable copy lives in Supabase.</p></div></body></html>`,
  },
}];

/* 10c — Record whether this match was actually stored.
 *
 * Every Supabase write (7a–7d, 10a, 10b) continues on error, which is right —
 * a database outage must not cost the coach their report — but it also means a
 * failed write looks exactly like a successful one. That is how reports went
 * unsaved on every run without anyone noticing. This node reads each write's
 * output and stamps the result onto the cached report, so node 12 serves it and
 * the frontend can say plainly when a report exists only in n8n's cache.
 */
const matchId = $('11 Format report').first().json.match_id;
const WRITES = ['7a Upsert club', '7b Upsert players', '7c Upsert match',
                '7d Upsert player stats', '10a Save player reports', '10b Save team report'];

const failures = [];
for (const name of WRITES) {
  let items;
  try {
    items = $(name).all();
  } catch (e) {
    failures.push(`${name}: did not run`);
    continue;
  }
  for (const item of items) {
    const err = item.json && item.json.error;
    if (err) failures.push(`${name}: ${err.description || err.message || 'write failed'}`);
  }
}

const stored = failures.length === 0;
const store = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');
if (store.reports && store.reports[matchId]) {
  store.reports[matchId].stored = stored;
  store.reports[matchId].storage_errors = failures;
}

return [{ json: { match_id: matchId, stored, storage_errors: failures } }];
